<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table  <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.2.1 General Models ‣ 4.2 Language Models ‣ 4 Experimental Setup ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents a concise overview of the LLMs evaluated in the study. It categorizes each model by name, parameter size, source type (open or closed), and the API service provider used to access them. The models include both proprietary and open-source systems. Proprietary models, such as various versions of Google’s Gemini (e.g., Gemini 2.5 Pro, Flash Preview, and Flash), and Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4, are closed-source, meaning their architectures and training details are not publicly available. These models are accessed through their respective API services, such as Google’s Gemini API and the Anthropic API.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, open-source models like DeepSeek R1 (236B), DeepSeek Chat (67B), LLaMA 3.3 70B, QWQ 32, and QWEN 3 32B offer more transparency in terms of model architecture and training datasets. These are made available through platforms such as the DeepSeek API, Together API, Nvidia API, and Deepinfra API.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The parameter sizes of the open-source models are explicitly stated, which is important for understanding their potential capabilities and computational requirements. The proprietary models do not disclose their parameter counts, reflecting the limited public insight into their underlying architectures.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, the table illustrates a diverse selection of LLMs sourced from both major tech companies and open research communities, providing a broad basis for comparative experimentation and analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
