</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generated model outputs using the Engineering prompt template <a href="#S10.F1" title="Template 1 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and the Evaluation prompt template <a href="#S10.F2" title="Template 2 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> separately.As shown in Table <a href="#S6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 6.2 Treatment ‣ 6 Results &amp; Discussion ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the average similarity scores, evaluated by a Llama 3.3 70B judge, are reported for eight models on the diagnosis task. The scores range from (78.0%) to (86.0%), indicating that all evaluated models demonstrate strong semantic alignment under the given prompts.The top-performing model, Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview (03-25), achieved the highest similarity score at (86.0%), highlighting the impact of recent architectural refinements or expanded training data. Close behind is QWQ-32, scoring (85.9%), effectively tying for second place and proving competitive despite limited adoption. Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17, Thinking) followed with a solid (85.0%), showing how variations in inference behavior (e.g., "Thinking" mode) can yield measurable gains in semantic alignment. At the other end of the spectrum, Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17), without the "Thinking" mode, recorded the lowest score at
(78.0%), underperforming relative to its sibling variants. Deepseek-chat scored (82.7%), placing it above the lowest performer but still trailing the top contenders. Mid-tier results included DeepSeek-R1 (84.2%), Llama 3.3 70B (83.6%), and Gemini 2.0 Flash (83.1%), all delivering solid, if not leading, performance. Overall, the results span a compact range of 8.0 percentage points, from (78.0%) to (86.0%), indicating a generally strong level of performance across all models. However, the standout scores from newer or enhanced models, especially Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview, underscore the benefits of continual optimization in both prompt design and model development.</p>
</div>
</section>
