</figure>
<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generated model outputs using the Engineering prompt template <a href="#S10.F17" title="Template 17 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> and the Evaluation prompt template <a href="#S10.F18" title="Template 18 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> separately.As show in table  <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 6.1 Diagnosis ‣ 6 Results &amp; Discussion ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> all eight models deliver moderately high similarity scores for their treatment recommendations, ranging from (77.4 %) to (82.9 %). The Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17, Thinking) led the set at (82.9 %), followed closely by Llama 3.3 70B at (82.3 %) and QWQ-32 at (82.1 %). Deepseek-chat achieved (81.91 %), while the secondary Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17) variant score (81.0 %). Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview (03-25) and Deepseek-R1 recorded (80.5 %) and (79.9%), respectively, with the original Gemini 2.0 Flash trailing at (77.4 %). The spread of (5.49 %) between the top and bottom performers highlights a meaningful performance gap in generating treatment plans. The clear advantage of the Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17, Thinking) suggests that its latest reasoning capabilities particularly enhance clinical coherence and relevance. Llama 3.3 70B and QWQ-32 also demonstrate that robust language understanding and contextual breadth translate into more accurate treatment outputs, marking them as strong baselines for further development.At the lower end, Gemini 2.0 Flash’s (77.4% ) score underscores how quickly performance can lag without iterative updates, while Deepseek-R1’s sub-80% result indicates potential weaknesses in domain-specific knowledge or recommendation specificity. Deepseek-chat’s solid upper-mid placement (81.9 %) shows that conversational optimization aids treatment advice, but it still falls short of models incorporating the newest architectural enhancements. Overall, these findings point to the importance of continuous model refinement to achieve clinically reliable treatment generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
