</figure>
<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the Engineering prompt template <a href="#S10.F5" title="Template 5 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> to generate the model outputs, and then evaluated them for accuracy in classification without using a separate evaluation prompt.As shown in Table <a href="#S6.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 6.4 Classification ‣ 6 Results &amp; Discussion ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> compares each model’s ability to assign both broad disorder categories and granular specific disorders using two metrics: F1-weighted score and subset accuracy. Across the board, models achieve higher scores on the broader category task F1-weighted scores range from (0.60) to (0.72), while subset accuracy spans (0.26) to (0.54). In contrast, performance on specific disorders is uniformly lower, with F1-weighted values between (0.37) and (0.50) and subset accuracy from (0.14) to (0.44). This pattern reflects the greater difficulty of exactly matching the full set of fine-grained labels for each case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">DeepSeek-R1 leads in the category classification task, posting the highest F1-weighted score of (0.72) and subset accuracy of (0.54). Close behind, Llama 3.3 70B and the Gemini 2.5 Flash (04-17) variant both achieve balanced category performance, Llama at (0.68)/(0.46) and Gemini Flash at (0.68)/(0.47). For specific disorders, DeepSeek-R1 again tops the field with (0.50) F1-weighted and (0.44) subset accuracy, indicating its relative strength in identifying multiple, co-occurring disorders. QWQ-32 and Gemini 2.0 Flash also perform respectably on the specific task, with F1-weighted scores of (0.45)-(0.46).</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The gap between category and specific-disorder scores, averaging around (0.20)-(0.25) F1 points, highlights the challenge of multi-label, fine-grained classification in clinical contexts. Models that excel at broad categorization still struggle to capture every nuanced diagnosis in a single pass, as evidenced by the lower subset accuracies across the board. These results underscore the need for targeted improvements, whether through additional domain data, hierarchical label modeling, or specialized prompt strategies to push LLMs toward clinically reliable, multi-label diagnostic performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.5 </span>Management Plan</h3>

