</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the Engineering prompt template <a href="#S10.F10" title="Template 10 ‣ 10.4 Prompt Templates ‣ 10 Appendix ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. As shown in Table <a href="#S6.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ 6.7 Mental QA ‣ 6 Results &amp; Discussion ‣ Psychiatry-Bench: A Multi-Task Benchmark for LLMs in Psychiatry" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, models’ average similarity scores under Prompt 1 range from (79.3 %) to (88.0 %), while under Prompt 2 they span (83.1 %) to (88.1 %). Deepseek-R1 remains near the top of both distributions with (88.0 %) and (88.1 %), respectively, and Deepseek-chat jumps from (82.7 %) to (88.1 %). At the lower end, the Gemini 2.5 Flash Preview (04-17, Thinking) rises from (79.3 %) to (85.9 %), whereas the Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview (03-25) declines from (87.0 %) to (84.6 %). These shifts underscore that definitional accuracy and its alignment with expert references varies substantially with prompt formulation.The magnitude of change varies by architecture. Deepseek-chat’s sizable +5.4 point gain and the Gemini 2.5 Flash (Thinking) model’s +6.6 point improvement highlight how enhanced instructional phrasing can bolster performance even in fact-based tasks. Conversely, the Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview’s -2.4 point drop demonstrates that a seemingly minor prompt tweak can grace alignment for some models. QWQ-32 (86.0 % → 84.3 %) and LLaMA 3.3 70B (84.2 % → 84.1 %) show minimal (&lt;1 point) fluctuations, indicating greater prompt robustness in these cases.Deepseek-R1’s near-identical scores across both prompts suggest it generalizes definitional reasoning most consistently. Overall, these results emphasize the critical role of prompt Engineeringing in terminology-focused QA: small changes in phrasing or structure can yield double-digit performance swings. For sensitive domains like psychiatry, ensuring prompt clarity and close alignment with a model’s instruction-following tendencies is essential to achieve reliable, clinically accurate definitions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.8 </span>Sequential Question Answering</h3>

